<h2>The Bottom Line</h2>
<p>Scouts are watching the things you cannot see on a highlight reel. The scan. The decision. The reaction to a mistake. The way you carry yourself when nobody on your team can find a pass.</p>

<p>Those are the habits that get a 13 year old pulled into an academy after a 9 nil hammering. Those are the habits that get players noticed when everyone else is chasing tricks and clips.</p>

<p>Train them on purpose. Stop chasing the things scouts already told us do not matter long term.</p>

